# infinite_goodness: one could read "infinite" in S1 as filling all of reality, so that it leaves no room for its contrary. In S2 it could instead mean unlimited in perfection. But the text does not mark any such shift, and both statements read naturally as the same claim. So I have kept it as one sense.
